{"title":"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CanadaMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be positive integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c48917438fe4244b096d2b4174a675d1635f05f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d+e=2010$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"192\" height=\"14\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the largest of the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9bbeb7caa1770d1d3cb842655f27e245b08188f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/5/dd54f8129186e28453c8c19f0c38ca25420a8e9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f8719bd65794b7cadb653bb83b22fe2cc24c8cb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d+e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />. What is the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/6/7e67b119fa6fdbf592498cda62d6a5394e542da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 670 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 671 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 802 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 803 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 804$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"440\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We want to try make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9bbeb7caa1770d1d3cb842655f27e245b08188f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/5/dd54f8129186e28453c8c19f0c38ca25420a8e9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f8719bd65794b7cadb653bb83b22fe2cc24c8cb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d+e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" /> as close as possible so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, the maximum of these, is smallest.\n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6ec5b3fd58f4bcf1d450360db25a0492daad571c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2010=670+670+670$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"186\" height=\"14\" />. In order to express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/054090e60a5dcb8bc33213620b3af9278f9a3e12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2010$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> as a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers, we must split up some of these numbers. There are two ways to do this (while keeping the sum of two numbers as close as possible): <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/c/4cce121060e0e96aedae130b16e474e2d2965229.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2010=670+1+670+1+668$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"248\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/48265cfb50f279cd9624e038cb3b524f2a3152f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2010=670+1+669+1+669$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"248\" height=\"14\" />. We see that in both cases, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2b5b001d120ed78f226ed5d50b1b1c06b490cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$671$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/e/59ede54510cf517513917fd4e24cc80e045ac9b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$671 \\Rightarrow \\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/3/283da71e258cd47678acef397f40472ab91ea8bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b \\le M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/a/dba672c43864c7fb65f959199d2ec275ebeb6cd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d + e \\le M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/637df5552de7cd5252a1f443578a8c03103c42b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &lt; b + c \\le M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/1/501177a58e66386c4ddac17a0451d98fb40b0f56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2010 = a + b + c + d + e &lt; 3M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"245\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/5/3c5d1fcc4649ea6eb4b097ba553c19dedae5faa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M &gt; 670$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/c/aacae1b8d34bfd59bac9190aaa5c638d0951a565.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M \\ge 671$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>For the values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/e/8beeed4cd296de20c52c8e966cca6434aad177c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c,d,e) = (669,1,670,1,669)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"258\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/0/7805d226d85abf8b00cb9829b41955f2b84ab120.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = 671$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, so the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e22fe9583d5df5c630aa8986b32f508a03ecb545.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{671}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />. The answer is (B).\n</p><p>~ math31415926535\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that only the sums of adjacent numbers matter. (For example, a &amp; c could be extremely high, as long as b is relatively low.)\nTherefore creating \"mountains\" and \"valleys\" is the best way to lower the sum of adjacent numbers. We can do\n</p><p><br />\n1. (high, low, high, low, high)\n</p><p><br />\nor\n</p><p><br />\n2. (low, high, low, high, low)\n</p><p><br />\nIn the extreme case that each \"low\" = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/054090e60a5dcb8bc33213620b3af9278f9a3e12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2010$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> will be divided into either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers for cases 1 and 2, respectively. Obviously dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will yield a lower number, so we consider case 1.\n</p><p>Dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/054090e60a5dcb8bc33213620b3af9278f9a3e12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2010$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a4cf3ebb294df5e93003bf9de36ea15cab3b818.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$670$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, or\n</p><p><br />\n(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/2/8820305b451ac6fe4521ede030db85b24aad168c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$670, 0, 670, 0, 670$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />)\n</p><p><br />\nHowever, all five numbers must be positive, and the closest we can get to this is\n</p><p><br />\n(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a26cc848ad2bfa508615d4032149b784050f4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$668, 3, 668, 3, 668$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />)\n</p><p><br />\nThe lowest possible sum of two adjacent numbers then becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2b5b001d120ed78f226ed5d50b1b1c06b490cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$671$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath\">Video Solution by CanadaMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CanadaMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/RDqm4GrKGyg?si=h7nKbYsKG-Yd8UFA&amp;t=506\">https://youtu.be/RDqm4GrKGyg?si=h7nKbYsKG-Yd8UFA&amp;t=506</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B\">2010 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017181309\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 343/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8595/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.558      1 -total\n 59.58%    7.482      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 38.62%    4.850      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8826:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017181309 and revision id 262430. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}